OPTIMIZATION 5: SORT FIX (benchmark/genetic_benchmark.cpp, insertionSortPrograms)

WHY
- Cancer scaled poorly with OpenMP (1.5x) and batching (1.07x), so profiled it separately.
- perf on cancer: program::operator= 11.2%, node::operator= 10.1%, malloc/free/new ~5%, node::node() 1.9%. Program copying ~28% of CPU time, more than execute_kernel (24%).
- Caller graph: 99% of program::operator= came from insertionSortPrograms (called from run_symbolic_classification).
- Runs on one core while the other 3 sit idle, so its wall-clock share is even larger than its CPU %.

PROBLEM
- Insertion sort on the program array itself. Every shift (programs[j + 1] = programs[j]) is a full deep copy: free old node array, allocate new one, construct and copy every node.
- Up to ~n^2/4 deep copies per sort.

CHANGE
- Sort an array of indices instead: std::iota fills idx = [0, 1, ..., n-1], then std::stable_sort orders idx by raw_fitness_.
- Then copy each program once into a temp vector in sorted order, and once back.
- Deep copies: ~n^2/4 -> exactly 2n. Sorting work: O(n^2) -> O(n log n) on integers.
- stable_sort keeps ties in original order, same as insertion sort, so the final order is identical.
- Function name kept so the 3 call sites don't change.

RESULTS (Opt 4 -> Opt 5, speedup; total speedup vs baseline)
- cancer:      11.6 s -> 6.06 s (1.91x); total 21x
- diabetes:    0.309 s -> 0.304 s (no change)
- housing:     4.43 s -> 4.45 s (no change)
- silk-wave:   9.9 s -> 9.8 s (no change)
- square-wave: 28.6 s -> 28.8 s (no change)

CORRECTNESS
- Cancer full output (excluding timing) compared with Opt 4.
- [Add result of the all-stages check script with 05-sort-fix included.]

OBSERVATIONS
- ~10-line algorithmic fix nearly halved cancer's runtime.
- Only cancer benefited. The other benchmarks also call the sort, but its cost there is negligible: likely a smaller population size and/or a much larger evaluation cost per run, so the sort is a tiny share.
- Shows why profiling each benchmark separately matters: cancer's bottleneck was a completely different kind (serial algorithmic hotspot) than the others (evaluation speed).
